      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ✅ **LGTM** — All checks pass. [[trajectory](go/traj/e87fc329-ab79-44d5-b6ff-9c2537d0f5f4)]\n\n### Review Summary\n**Functionality \u0026 Security:**\n- The CL successfully resolves all heap buffer overflow vulnerabilities by delegating memory allocation and reallocation to Zephyr\u0027s native `k_heap_calloc` and `k_heap_realloc`. This securely handles `count * size` multiplication and safely bounds memory copies during reallocation.\n- `plat_calloc` cleanly wraps `sys_alloc`, avoiding redundant manual `memset` overhead since `k_heap_calloc` natively zero-initializes the allocated memory.\n- `sys_free` and `sys_alloc_usable_size` correctly handle `NULL` pointer inputs, which improves the overall robustness of the PAL APIs.\n\n**Style \u0026 Consistency:**\n- The code changes are concise, idiomatic, and adhere perfectly to Zephyr coding guidelines.\n- The use of `COND_CODE_1(CONFIG_ZTEST, (), (static))` is a clean way to expose internal functions to the test suite without polluting the global namespace.\n\n**Testing:**\n- The `ztest` suite provides comprehensive and rigorous coverage of the allocator logic.\n- Using `ztest_set_fault_valid(true)` to verify that intentional zero-sized allocations, integer multiplication overflows, and OOM conditions successfully trigger fatal panics (`k_oops()`) is an excellent defensive testing strategy.\n- Memory shrinking and growing behaviors for `realloc` are thoroughly verified.\n\nTAG\u003dagy\nCONV\u003de87fc329-ab79-44d5-b6ff-9c2537d0f5f4",
